      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That profound feeling of fundamental \"unbelonging\" is deeply painful and can feel all-encompassing. It suggests a struggle with self-worth and the pressure to conform to external definitions of \"right\" or \"right for this world.\" Consider that the desire to \"be right\" for the world is often self-imposed, and self-acceptance might require less focus on *becoming right* and more on *accepting what is inherent to you now",
